course: dictionary
lesson: 5149
title: Words for people and where they come from
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some nouns tell you who a person is and where they come from. «An Irishman» is a man who was born in Ireland, or whose family and home are Irish. The word man tells you it is a man, and Irish tells you the place.
explain: Context helps you here too. «His rhyme is "By means of a grating / I have stopped your ating"; Kipling says he was "an Hi-ber-ni-an" (an Irishman), joking that his accent made "eating" sound like "ating".» The joke is about how one man spoke, not a fact about every Irish person.
explain: Be careful with jokes that laugh at a whole nation. Old jokes like «an Englishman, an Irishman and a Scotsman» can be unkind, so think about who is being mocked. Today people often say «an Irish man» or «a man from Ireland», and use «Irishwoman» for a woman.
fact: «Irishman» means a man who was born in Ireland, or whose family and home are Irish.
fact: The plural is «Irishmen», meaning two or more men from Ireland.
fact: For a woman you say «Irishwoman»; for everyone you can say «the Irish» or «Irish people».
fact: Today people often say «an Irish man» or «a man from Ireland».
fact: Old jokes such as «an Englishman, an Irishman and a Scotsman» can mock a whole nation, so they can be unkind.
exercise: Mia's grandad was born in Ireland. What is he? | A Scotsman | An Irishwoman | A man from a Spanish village | *An Irishman
exercise: Which word means a woman who was born in Ireland? | Englishwoman | Irishman | Irishmen | *Irishwoman
exercise: «The Irishman told a joke about his accent.» Find and copy the word that names where the man comes from. | told | joke | accent | *Irishman
test: Which phrase do people often use today for a man from Ireland? | A green hat | Irishmen only | An old Irish joke | *A man from Ireland
test: Which words mean Irish people as a whole? | Irishwoman | *the Irish | Irishman
exam: Why should we think before repeating an old joke like «an Englishman, an Irishman and a Scotsman»? | It is only for children | It has no meaning at all | *It may mock a whole nation, which can be unkind | It is always funny
